{"entryType": "UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)", "primaryAccession": "Q15825", "secondaryAccessions": ["B2R8V4", "B4DQH1"], "uniProtkbId": "ACHA6_HUMAN", "entryAudit": {"firstPublicDate": "1997-11-01", "lastAnnotationUpdateDate": "2026-06-10", "lastSequenceUpdateDate": "1997-11-01", "entryVersion": 212, "sequenceVersion": 1}, "annotationScore": 5.0, "organism": {"scientificName": "Homo sapiens", "commonName": "Human", "taxonId": 9606, "lineage": ["Eukaryota", "Metazoa", "Chordata", "Craniata", "Vertebrata", "Euteleostomi", "Mammalia", "Eutheria", "Euarchontoglires", "Primates", "Haplorrhini", "Catarrhini", "Hominidae", "Homo"]}, "proteinExistence": "1: Evidence at protein level", "proteinDescription": {"recommendedName": {"fullName": {"value": "Neuronal acetylcholine receptor subunit alpha-6"}}, "flag": "Precursor"}, "genes": [{"geneName": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000312", "source": "HGNC", "id": "HGNC:15963"}], "value": "CHRNA6"}}], "comments": [{"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "Q9R0W9"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "16835356"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305", "source": "PubMed", "id": "16835356"}], "value": "Component of neuronal acetylcholine receptors (nAChRs) that function as pentameric, ligand-gated cation channels with high calcium permeability among other activities. nAChRs are excitatory neurotrasnmitter receptors formed by a collection of nAChR subunits known to mediate synaptic transmission in the nervous system and the neuromuscular junction. Each nAchR subunit confers differential attributes to channel properties, including activation, deactivation and desensitization kinetics, pH sensitivity, cation permeability, and binding to allosteric modulators (Probable). CHRNA6 forms pentameric channels with CHRNB2, CHRNB3 and CHRNA4 that exhibit high sensitivity to ACh and nicotine and are predominantly expressed in only a few brain areas, including dopaminergic neurons, norepirephrine neurons and cells of the visual system (PubMed:16835356). nAChrs containing CHRNA6 subunits mediate endogenous cholinergic modulation of dopamine and gamma-aminobutyric acid (GABA) release in response to nicotine at nerve terminals"}], "commentType": "FUNCTION"}, {"commentType": "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY", "reaction": {"name": "Ca(2+)(in) = Ca(2+)(out)", "reactionCrossReferences": [{"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA:29671"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:29108"}], "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "P43681"}]}}, {"commentType": "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY", "reaction": {"name": "K(+)(in) = K(+)(out)", "reactionCrossReferences": [{"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA:29463"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:29103"}], "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "P02709"}]}}, {"commentType": "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY", "reaction": {"name": "Na(+)(in) = Na(+)(out)", "reactionCrossReferences": [{"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA:34963"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:29101"}], "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "P02709"}]}}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "Q9R0W9"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "16835356"}], "value": "Activated by a myriad of ligands such as acetylcholine, cytisine and nicotine (PubMed:16835356). CHRNA6 nAChR activity is inhibited by the antagonists alpha-conotoxin MII and PIA, a small disulfide-constrained peptides from cone snails"}], "commentType": "ACTIVITY REGULATION"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "Q9R0W9"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "16835356"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "27344019"}], "value": "Neuronal AChR is composed of two different types of subunits: alpha and non-alpha (beta). CHRNA6/alpha-6 subunit can be combined to CHRNB2/beta-2, CHRNA4/alpha-4 and CHRNB3/beta-3 to give rise to functional receptors (PubMed:16835356). Heteropentamers containing CHRNB3 have an stoichiometry of (CHRNA6:CHRNB2)2:CHRNB3 (PubMed:16835356). Interacts with LYPD6 (PubMed:27344019)"}], "commentType": "SUBUNIT"}, {"commentType": "SUBCELLULAR LOCATION", "subcellularLocations": [{"location": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "Q9R0W9"}], "value": "Synaptic cell membrane", "id": "SL-0531"}, "topology": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255"}], "value": "Multi-pass membrane protein", "id": "SL-9909"}}]}, {"commentType": "ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS", "events": ["Alternative splicing"], "isoforms": [{"name": {"value": "1"}, "isoformIds": ["Q15825-1"], "isoformSequenceStatus": "Displayed"}, {"name": {"value": "2"}, "isoformIds": ["Q15825-2"], "sequenceIds": ["VSP_042713"], "isoformSequenceStatus": "Described"}]}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305"}], "value": "Belongs to the ligand-gated ion channel (TC 1.A.9) family. Acetylcholine receptor (TC 1.A.9.1) subfamily. Alpha-6/CHRNA6 sub-subfamily"}], "commentType": "SIMILARITY"}], "features": [{"type": "Signal", "location": {"start": {"value": 1, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 25, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255"}]}, {"type": "Chain", "location": {"start": {"value": 26, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 494, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "Neuronal acetylcholine receptor subunit alpha-6", "featureId": "PRO_0000000360"}, {"type": "Topological domain", "location": {"start": {"value": 26, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 239, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "Extracellular"}, {"type": "Transmembrane", "location": {"start": {"value": 240, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 264, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "Helical", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255"}]}, {"type": "Transmembrane", "location": {"start": {"v